WEBVTT


00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.700
Lifelines can save you grief
just in case disaster strikes.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:11.600
At the point where you want to insert
a lifeline, pull out all of the

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.740
needles just slightly, keeping the
stitches in the hooks of the needles.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.210
Thread a darning needle or a double-eye
needle with a smooth contrasting

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:25.670
color thread or yarn, leaving the
stitches and the hooks of the needles.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.610
Pull the strand through each stitch.

00:00:29.085 --> 00:00:32.985
Continue running the strand
through each stitch across the row.

00:00:33.135 --> 00:00:37.335
If the work dropped off the needles at
this point, the stitches would be secure.

00:00:37.394 --> 00:00:41.235
Continue knitting according to
your pattern, ignoring the strand.

00:00:41.745 --> 00:00:45.435
If disaster strikes, you can
confidently drop the work from the

00:00:45.435 --> 00:00:48.855
machine and tear out to that lifeline.

00:00:49.305 --> 00:00:53.625
Carefully pick up each stitch,
leaving the lifeline in place.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:56.450
Then you can continue knitting.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:02.390
Again, leaving the lifeline in place, just
in case when you've finished knitting the

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:05.330
piece, the lifeline will slip out easily.

